# vdbactivatefrompoints

- Label: VDB Activate from Points
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2048
- Parameters: 16 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vdbactivatefrompoints.html
- Summary (EN): Turns on the leaves of a VDB that contain points from one or more point clouds. The reference VDB sets the original size and origin of the result.
- Résumé (FR) : Active les feuilles d'un VDB qui contiennent des points de nuages de points, en gardant la taille et l'origine du VDB de référence.

- Inputs meaning: ["refvdb: reference VDB; its origin and voxel size are the starting point", "activate_pts1: one or more geometry inputs; any leaf containing one of their points is activated"]

- Key parameters: ["Leaf Dilation: expands the active region by a fixed number of leaves", "Leaf Dilation Dist: expands the active region by a world-space distance rounded to the nearest leaf; the larger of this and Leaf Dilation is used", "Voxel Scale: scales the reference voxel size to produce a higher or lower resolution VDB", "Sort Leaves: makes leaf processing order repeatable, at extra time cost", "Clip Min X/Y/Z and Clip Max X/Y/Z: deactivate leaves whose world positions fall outside the bounds"]

- Caveats: ["Leaf order is non-deterministic by default; enable Sort Leaves if the algorithm depends on processing order", "Reads optional point attributes: integer invalid (non-zero means the point is ignored) and integer dilation (packs per-direction dilation hints)"]

